// Operator and punctuation matching.
//
// GENERATED by bootstrap/generator/gen_tables.py from
// meta/specs/LEXICAL_REFERENCE.md section 5.
//
// LONGEST MATCH FIRST, which is the whole content of the table: `<=>` must
// beat `<=`, `..*` must beat `..`, `=>!` must beat `=>`, and `!!!` must beat
// `!`. Trying shortest-first would silently produce a different program.
//
// The positional `!` rule (D-046) falls out of this for free: `!!!` matches as
// one token, `!=` as one, and a lone `!` as negation. There is no `!!`
// operator -- after D-001 removed sys!!! and asm!!! the tier marker
// distinguished nothing -- so `!!` is simply two negations, which is not an
// error at all.

